  <!-- TAKEAWAY -->
  <div class="takeaway animate">
    <div class="takeaway-label">// Key Insight</div>
    <p class="takeaway-text">Training a frontier LLM is not primarily a software problem — it is a <strong>capital allocation problem</strong>. The organizations that can fund $100M+ compute runs, negotiate petabyte-scale data licenses, and sustain 12–18 month development cycles are a vanishingly small group. This creates structural concentration in who can build, and therefore who can shape, the most capable AI systems.</p>
